// Rejection case (decimal summand): the aggregation summand must be a `Long`.
// Here `sum s` adds together `s`, bound to the decimal field `input.score`.
// Dogwood arithmetic operates only on `Long` values, not decimals — matching
// Cedar, whose +, -, * operate only on Long and offer no decimal arithmetic.
// Leaving a decimal summand unchecked is therefore unsafe: there is no defined
// meaning for summing decimals, so different implementations could reasonably
// choose different behavior.
//
// The summand's type was never checked, so this validated cleanly. It should
// be rejected by the temporal type-checker.
//
// Expected: rejected at `validate`.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    exists (n: Long). (
        (sum s for (s: decimal). where (Drupe::Action::"Charge"::request{ input.score: s })) == n
        && n > 0
    )
};
